+## Offline evidence binding review candidate
+
+[`tweetLunaEvidenceBinding.ts`](./tweetLunaEvidenceBinding.ts) exports `proposeLunaEvidenceBindingReview`, a pure offline correction-proposal function. It is not imported by the runtime caller, transport or CLI. Its explicit caller-selected policy is `luna-unique-exact-quote-review-v1`; omitting it leaves the function disabled before reading the request or response. The strict model schema, prompt/version and automatic validation are unchanged. This policy does not grant any dispatch, correction-application or production authority.
+
+The caller supplies the **original prepared dated identity request** and **unaltered model output text** from a retained receipt. The function validates the request/identity binding, parses the existing strict goalie schema, and searches the original source for each exact quote. Missing or multiple matches (including overlapping matches) reject the entire proposal. It never uses the model's wrong coordinates to choose among matches, changes quote text, normalizes case/whitespace/Unicode, repairs identity, fills an omission or changes a status. JavaScript string offsets are UTF-16; the existing exact-span validator also rejects surrogate/grapheme splits.
+
+For a unique match it derives `[start, start + text.length)` and reruns the unchanged goalie validator across all proposals: supplied goalie/subject/candidate binding, overlap, full-source negation/conditions, tentative wording, repeated identities, correction markers and other existing gates. Any failure returns no partial candidate. A valid original needs no correction. Only a changed coordinate pair that survives those gates becomes `candidate_for_human_review`.
+
+The immutable result retains the original model output text verbatim, its UTF-8 SHA256, request/source hashes, exact before/proposed spans and a version-bound candidate hash. Derived statuses stay nested under `candidate`, with `verified:false`, null game/team/override and source/game/conflict holds. `canApply:false`, `original_response_remains_held` and `evidence_binding_human_review_required` prevent this record from purporting to apply a change. The paid evaluation's historical score/result is never replaced by this candidate.
+
+This candidate resolves only quote coordinates. It cannot prove a unique quote expresses the intended claim or resolve complex semantics missed by existing finite wording guards. Source provenance, completed provider receipt, retention/packet lineage, reviewer identity/time/decision and source/game acceptance remain required at any future integration boundary. This module has no acceptance or persistence endpoint, UI, automated training path or consumer that lifts holds. Automatic rebinding would change the acceptance contract and needs separate explicit coordination, independent review, versioning and tests. See the [offline binding-review handoff](../../../tasks/artifacts/luna-reference-package-2026-10-31/span-binding-review/HANDOFF.md).
